From 7c1bc3ba0064dd282d475643d757e0b8d8b3789c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 20:53:15 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] refactor(sim): a field column's floor under a cut reads
 exactly by the monotone law

#637 step E1. Every tool Stock::simulate builds spans the verdict world
above its tip, so its swept solid holds every point above any point it
holds: a column's material is one interval [shell floor, tool bottom] or
nothing, and a cut from above never raises the floor. SdfField::column_span
reads both sides: the down-march's Top proves the shell floor; NoMaterial
is cut through or a sub-cell sliver, told apart by the cut layer's own
ray-entry record at the cell below the floor plane. A tool that does not
span (a truncated taper, a bare ball, a lathe sweep, a posed axis) sets
bounded_cuts and keeps step B's CutFromBelow refusal. floor_at keeps its
API; CarriedField::column_body now carries through-holes and slivers
instead of refusing the carry.

The step E design (the holders' mutation path, baking the turn's signed
permutation into the bricks, the upward march) is on the issue and in
docs/decisions/637-carried-stock-field.md; E2a-c are #779, #780, #781.

Nothing shipped changes: the column engine stays the default and the
field's down-march is untouched.

Refs #637
Refs #26

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
